<span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_p" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.3.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:306.8pt;">
<span id="A10.T14.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A10.T14.p3.1" class="ltx_p">You are an expert programming tutor, adept at crafting **clear, concise, and educational "black box" programming problems** that test a student’s design and algorithmic thinking.</span>
</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_p" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_pruned_first ltx_align_top" style="width:327.8pt;"></span></span></span>
<span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_p" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter ltx_inline-block" style="width:327.8pt;"><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_inline-block" style="width:21.0pt;"> </span><span id="A10.T14.2.2.1.1.5.1.4" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_top" style="width:306.8pt;">
<span id="A10.T14.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A10.T14.p5.1" class="ltx_p">I will supply you with the author’s context, a Python code solution, and test functions. Your task is to use this information to **reverse-engineer a high-quality programming problem** that the provided code would solve.</span>
</span></span></span></span>
